{
  "id": "QP01Z",
  "version": "2.0",
  "title": "Laryngoscopy",
  "description": "Laryngoscopy uses a specialized scope to visualize your voice box (larynx) for diagnosis or treatment of voice, throat, or breathing problems. The procedure may be diagnostic (to identify the cause of hoarseness, throat pain, or breathing difficulty) or therapeutic (to remove polyps, nodules, or treat other conditions). Your doctor can perform laryngoscopy using a flexible scope (less invasive) or rigid scope (allowing more treatment options). The procedure is relatively quick, minimally uncomfortable, and provides valuable information about laryngeal health.",
